# Expectation record for 09_optimization_levels/008_folded_vs_runtime_equivalence.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 008_folded_vs_runtime_equivalence
area               = 09_optimization_levels
description        = The same computation spelled over constants and over volatile operands, asserted equal
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Both spellings compute the same value over operands that stay inside the range of their
type, so no signed overflow occurs, every divisor is nonzero and every shift count is in
range.  The volatile spelling forces the backend to emit real instructions, which is what
makes the equality a comparison of the folder against the code generator rather than of
the folder against itself.  No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
int  folded=95 runtime=95 equal=1
uns  folded=8043744 runtime=8043744 equal=1
wide folded=109013499946 runtime=109013499946 equal=1
rel  folded=20 runtime=20 equal=1
cond folded=24 runtime=24 equal=1
all_equal=1
END
